From 8c9269bf355763d4ec8eea31ba114ce88cb852ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ROG HDR contributors <rog-hdr@invalid>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 08:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] keep devices carrying a network filesystem up through suspend

NetworkManager takes managed hardware devices down when the system
prepares to sleep, before the kernel freezes user tasks. A task blocked
in a buffered read of a hard NFS or SMB mount then waits on a page lock
that only the outstanding READ can release; with the transport gone it
never freezes and the kernel refuses to suspend (-EBUSY).

Treat a device that routes to the server of a mounted network
filesystem like a Wake-on-LAN device: skip it before sleep and re-check
it on wake. The links such a device depends on (VLAN parent, bridge
or bond ports) are kept too. Version 1.58.1-1ubuntu3+rogsleep1.
